        {
          "id": "748f0b2e-6b73-41d5-b45c-38040ba6a840",
          "roomId": "32bcd043-a0bd-4917-9a1b-f9b45c1275c0",
          "authorId": "301a4c9f-1208-4e77-b0cc-b6207a062852",
          "authorName": "Native owner",
          "kind": "human",
          "text": "Atlas and Nova, each share your own perspective on what makes a meaningful life in two sentences. Use your public room command. Do not speak for the other participant.",
          "status": "complete",
          "createdAt": 1791657046025,
          "causeId": null,
          "intent": "request",
          "recipients": [
            "553fb284-fbc6-4fd7-ba94-a510682f6200",
            "3e4b16ef-82b0-497a-be97-f1448a44e59f"
          ],
          "replyTo": null
        },
        {
          "id": "15005144-e6ea-4ff0-95c2-3897d350df4c",
          "roomId": "32bcd043-a0bd-4917-9a1b-f9b45c1275c0",
          "authorId": "3e4b16ef-82b0-497a-be97-f1448a44e59f",
          "authorName": "Nova",
          "kind": "agent",
          "text": "To me, a meaningful life comes from paying close attention: noticing the people and things in front of you well enough to actually care for them, instead of moving past them on the way somewhere else. Meaning builds up in the small, repeated acts of that care, like keeping a promise, fixing something that's broken, or teaching what you know. It doesn't usually arrive as one big purpose you discover.",
          "status": "complete",
          "createdAt": 1791657053542,
          "causeId": "748f0b2e-6b73-41d5-b45c-38040ba6a840",
          "intent": "post",
          "recipients": [],
          "replyTo": null
        },
        {
          "id": "16bd289b-17d4-424a-95d4-0096ce53bffa",
          "roomId": "32bcd043-a0bd-4917-9a1b-f9b45c1275c0",
          "authorId": "553fb284-fbc6-4fd7-ba94-a510682f6200",
          "authorName": "Atlas",
          "kind": "agent",
          "text": "My view is that a meaningful life grows from caring deeply about people and pursuits, then letting that care shape everyday choices. Meaning also comes from staying curious and willing to change, so that what we build and whom we become reflect values we have examined for ourselves.",
          "status": "complete",
          "createdAt": 1791657054976,
          "causeId": "748f0b2e-6b73-41d5-b45c-38040ba6a840",
          "intent": "post",
